digraph boys2foursNotreDame {NotreDame [URL="boys2foursNotreDame.html"];Nobles [URL="boys2foursNobles.html"];Hotchkiss [URL="boys2foursHotchkiss.html"];StMarks [URL="boys2foursStMarks.html"];Hopkins [URL="boys2foursHopkins.html"];GreenwichCountryDay [URL="boys2foursGreenwichCountryDay.html"];Middletown [URL="boys2foursMiddletown.html"];Hotchkiss -> NotreDame[label="38.6
05/16", weight="62", tooltip="NEIRA Boys & Girls Fours,Hopkins, Hotchkiss, Notre DameHousatonic Sprints			
Distance: 1500 Conditions: Sunny and beautiful morning, light quartering tailwind about 6mph, increasing to 9mph by the last race. Floating start. Comments: Boats raced top down, interleaving boys and girls heats. In the B1 race both Hotchkiss and Hopkins pushed starboard towards Notre Dame's lane, which eventually pinched the Notre Dame boat and caused it to hit the 1000m buoy. Notre Dame came to a stop and lost time untangling. The incident affected the Notre Dame B1 margin.
Thank you, Hotchkiss and Notre Dame for coming and enjoying the day with us! We look forward to hosting you again next year!
